WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.000
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:00.080 --> 00:01.310
[Viewer discretion is advised due to violence, self-harm, and potentially triggering scenes.] [Exclusive: Faceless singer Yul suspected of involvement in classmate's disappearance]

3
00:01.550 --> 00:02.080
[No wonder he doesn't show his face.]

4
00:02.080 --> 00:02.580
[This student used to work part-time at our store. No wonder he never gave me his ID.]

5
00:02.580 --> 00:03.090
[Could the disappearance mean he killed someone and buried them?] [He definitely killed someone.]

6
00:03.210 --> 00:04.490
[Reported] [Could he be the murderer?] [Definitely a murderer.] [Gonna leave the industry.] [Yul eliminated.] [Show your face.] [His classmates should come out and say something.] [I was a fan. How disappointing.]

7
00:05.660 --> 00:06.950
[[Breaking News] Expected release of interviews with classmates at the time]

8
00:07.270 --> 00:08.580
[[Update] Obtained testimonies from school personnel at the time of the incident] [[Breaking News] Expected release of interviews with classmates at the time]

9
00:08.760 --> 00:10.170
[Yul missing case] [Faceless singer Yul suspected of involvement in classmate's disappearance] [Popular faceless singer Yul allegedly involved in classmate's missing persons case]

10
00:10.180 --> 00:34.450
[Interviews with classmates regarding rookie singer Yul's past school violence controversy]

11
00:10.680 --> 00:13.180
That Yul is Lee Hanyul.

12
00:13.440 --> 00:14.820
He was our schoolmate.

13
00:15.240 --> 00:18.570
As far as I know, Lee Hanyul and Adolph were really close.

14
00:18.980 --> 00:20.310
I even have a video,

15
00:20.430 --> 00:21.760
taken in the school gym.

16
00:21.850 --> 00:24.010
The way Lee Hanyul treated him...

17
00:24.250 --> 00:27.730
Anyway, Adolph disappeared after that.

18
00:27.880 --> 00:29.870
I heard he might be dead.

19
00:30.740 --> 00:32.000
Lee Hanyul killed him.

20
00:32.000 --> 00:34.370
Killed his own friend. What a psycho.

21
00:35.240 --> 00:36.940
Suppress the video.

22
00:37.060 --> 00:40.040
Find those two bastards in the video claiming to be Hanyul's classmates first.

23
00:40.040 --> 00:42.770
Once you find them, bring them to me immediately.

24
00:52.370 --> 00:53.400
Hey, Pan.

25
00:54.010 --> 00:55.710
You're with Hanyul now, right?

26
00:55.710 --> 00:57.310
I'm going to find Hanyul now.

27
01:19.440 --> 01:21.170
Our Lee Won has grown wings,

28
01:21.600 --> 01:23.450
even stabbing me in the back.

29
01:24.490 --> 01:25.820
It's amazing, isn't it?

30
01:26.440 --> 01:29.270
It doesn't even take a day to ruin someone.

31
01:29.420 --> 01:34.280
Ah, and the one being ruined is me—

32
01:36.770 --> 01:39.240
Not that damn little brat.

33
01:45.020 --> 01:47.550
Now everyone knows that kid

34
01:47.670 --> 01:50.750
was brought up single-handedly by our company's CEO, composer Lee Won.

35
01:50.750 --> 01:51.990
I'm the one bearing all the losses,

36
01:51.990 --> 01:53.039
don't you think?

37
02:03.260 --> 02:04.920
Back then, his parents...

38
02:05.050 --> 02:07.820
How much did they sell that kid for?

39
02:08.380 --> 02:09.550
Do you remember?

40
02:10.530 --> 02:11.750
Let me think.

41
02:12.560 --> 02:14.880
It was about 10 million won back then.

42
02:15.000 --> 02:17.950
Considering inflation, it should be about

43
02:18.070 --> 02:19.590
a billion now?

44
02:22.490 --> 02:23.940
Thanks, Won.

45
02:24.340 --> 02:28.140
Thank you for helping me find the rascal who owed me a billion

46
02:28.280 --> 02:30.150
and ran away from me.

47
02:31.440 --> 02:33.020
He's in good health, right?

48
02:33.370 --> 02:35.320
Doesn't smoke or drink, right?

49
02:35.470 --> 02:38.840
After all, every organ of his is a precious commodity.

50
02:39.650 --> 02:40.880
All right.

51
02:41.870 --> 02:44.070
Now it's time to keep your promise, Won.

52
02:44.640 --> 02:47.530
That thing you promised me.

53
02:50.550 --> 02:51.740
[Collateral Contract Name: Kim Jaeseok]

54
02:52.670 --> 02:54.040
Ten million won.

55
02:55.540 --> 02:58.390
Just a kid, what use can he be?

56
02:59.460 --> 03:02.000
We'll use him as bait for the next plan.

57
03:02.140 --> 03:03.300
Lock him up first.

58
03:05.020 --> 03:06.610
I'm scared.

59
03:07.530 --> 03:08.930
Where's Mom?

60
03:12.410 --> 03:13.500
Boss,

61
03:14.150 --> 03:16.320
this kid doesn't belong here.

62
03:21.500 --> 03:22.590
Won,

63
03:23.890 --> 03:24.930
do you know him?

64
03:25.150 --> 03:26.110
No,

65
03:26.370 --> 03:27.400
I don't know him.

66
03:27.910 --> 03:29.180
Then why?

67
03:29.780 --> 03:31.370
Please give me some time,

68
03:31.680 --> 03:35.950
until this kid grows up enough to be useful.

69
03:43.050 --> 03:46.010
Then what do I get in the meantime?

70
03:46.480 --> 03:48.810
I'll do anything.

71
03:49.380 --> 03:52.090
I'll do his share too.

72
03:52.390 --> 03:53.480
Please.

73
03:55.810 --> 03:56.890
All right then.

74
03:57.340 --> 03:59.480
This is the first time our Won has begged me.

75
03:59.480 --> 04:01.160
I have to grant your request.

76
04:02.000 --> 04:04.520
Then starting today,

77
04:04.660 --> 04:08.240
you'll be responsible for that kid's share.

78
04:18.820 --> 04:20.279
I did as you said.

79
04:20.600 --> 04:22.890
I waited for him to grow up,

80
04:23.110 --> 04:24.790
but that kid suddenly ran away.

81
04:24.790 --> 04:25.830
Right?

82
04:26.990 --> 04:28.050
Bring him here—

83
04:28.210 --> 04:30.500
right now, immediately.

84
04:32.780 --> 04:34.490
Just give me a week.

85
04:41.150 --> 04:43.560
Whether it was back then or now—

86
04:45.260 --> 04:48.870
what does that kid mean to you, Won?

87
04:50.650 --> 04:52.750
I'm begging you for the last time.

88
05:00.120 --> 05:02.250
If he disappears like he did back then,

89
05:03.270 --> 05:05.500
you'll have to pay me 3 times as much—no—

90
05:08.660 --> 05:11.120
you'll have to pay me dozens of times as much.

91
05:21.860 --> 05:24.140
Your parents sold you to me

92
05:24.310 --> 05:26.050
for a mere 5 million won.

93
05:36.140 --> 05:39.140
You should be of great use.

94
05:48.830 --> 05:55.420
[Some scenes were created with AI.]

95
05:57.659 --> 06:01.400
[Adapted from the webtoon "The Sound of Sugar Cubes" by Kim Tak]

96
06:01.400 --> 06:04.200
[Screenwriter: So-on (JD)]

97
06:04.210 --> 06:07.180
[Director: Yoon Jinyoung]

98
06:23.640 --> 06:25.250
[Yoo Dohyun]

99
06:25.250 --> 06:26.840
[Cho Chanhyeon]

100
06:26.850 --> 06:28.540
[Ko Gyeol]

101
06:29.990 --> 06:33.440
[The Sound of Sugar Cubes]

102
06:47.530 --> 06:48.930
These darn reporters...

103
06:49.340 --> 06:50.320
Damn it.

104
06:51.710 --> 06:52.690
Forget it.

105
07:04.290 --> 07:09.870
Why is the hourly wage for handing out flyers so low lately?

106
07:10.220 --> 07:12.030
How is anyone supposed to make a living?

107
07:12.030 --> 07:12.570
Right?

108
07:12.730 --> 07:15.150
Life is too hard.

109
07:16.710 --> 07:18.630
It's too hard, paying so little.

110
07:19.000 --> 07:20.430
Excuse me.

111
07:21.260 --> 07:22.390
Damn it.

112
07:35.180 --> 07:36.380
Hey, hey.

113
07:36.820 --> 07:38.710
You want to go out?

114
07:38.830 --> 07:40.460
They came for me.

115
07:41.720 --> 07:43.800
I don't want to cause you trouble.

116
07:44.050 --> 07:46.810
So what? Will going out now solve the problem?

117
07:49.230 --> 07:51.030
Lee Won will be here soon.

118
07:51.360 --> 07:53.350
Regardless of if he's here to save the day or ruin it—

119
07:53.350 --> 07:55.320
anyway, he'll definitely come.

120
07:55.470 --> 07:56.850
Just sit down and wait for him, you brat.

121
07:56.850 --> 07:57.850
Seriously.

122
07:58.420 --> 07:59.940
You scared me.

123
08:01.580 --> 08:02.460
How did you get in?

124
08:02.460 --> 08:04.660
There are a bunch of reporters outside.

125
08:04.900 --> 08:06.630
I came in through the back door.

126
08:07.130 --> 08:09.060
How do you know about the back door?

127
08:09.150 --> 08:10.800
I've been here so many times.

128
08:11.350 --> 08:12.500
I see.

129
08:12.850 --> 08:15.250
But now this back door is as good as gone.

130
08:15.550 --> 08:16.450
Why?

131
08:16.910 --> 08:18.360
Those reporters saw me.

132
08:19.860 --> 08:23.260
You brat, you're here to ruin things.

133
08:23.470 --> 08:26.130
You've completely turned us into rats in a trap.

134
08:26.280 --> 08:27.320
Damn it.

135
08:38.120 --> 08:39.909
Why did you risk coming here?

136
08:41.750 --> 08:44.350
Getting involved with me won't do you any good.

137
08:46.140 --> 08:48.470
I love getting involved with you the most.

138
08:49.110 --> 08:50.440
It excites me.

139
08:51.730 --> 08:53.160
Excites you?

140
08:54.370 --> 08:57.860
Well, given how thrilling the situation is now, I guess.

141
09:03.890 --> 09:05.010
Hanyul.

142
09:09.240 --> 09:10.770
Run away with me.

143
09:12.980 --> 09:14.050
What?

144
09:15.270 --> 09:17.000
I said let's run away together—

145
09:17.680 --> 09:19.140
to somewhere far away.

146
09:20.540 --> 09:22.650
To a place where no one can find us.

147
09:24.610 --> 09:25.840
I don't want to.

148
09:27.210 --> 09:29.120
I don't want to run anymore.

149
09:30.330 --> 09:34.930
I will never hide like a coward again.

150
09:38.780 --> 09:39.820
Good.

151
09:41.520 --> 09:43.520
That's the Lee Hanyul I know.

152
09:50.090 --> 09:52.430
Is something wrong with you?

153
10:00.410 --> 10:01.450
Pan.

154
10:04.080 --> 10:05.580
I have a favor to ask.

155
10:06.980 --> 10:08.580
Wh-What is it?

156
10:13.310 --> 10:14.940
It's Lee Hanyul.

157
10:16.140 --> 10:17.930
No, Lee Hanyul is over there.

158
10:18.050 --> 10:19.100
Lee Hanyul! Lee Hanyul!

159
10:19.100 --> 10:20.640
-Where? Where? -Here! Here! Lee Hanyul!

160
10:20.640 --> 10:21.870
-Lee Hanyul! -Hurry, hurry, hurry!

161
10:21.870 --> 10:22.900
Lee Hanyul!

162
10:23.310 --> 10:24.390
Catch him!

163
10:39.250 --> 10:40.760
Where are we going?

164
10:42.170 --> 10:43.830
I'm asking where we are going.

165
10:46.340 --> 10:47.620
To find Adolph.

166
10:48.710 --> 10:49.980
Adolph?

167
10:50.660 --> 10:51.650
Yeah.

168
11:36.310 --> 11:37.680
He's sleeping.

169
11:38.880 --> 11:40.880
He was in a coma before.

170
11:41.120 --> 11:43.060
He just woke up not long ago.

171
11:44.730 --> 11:46.200
Why...

172
11:46.830 --> 11:48.390
Why is he here...

173
11:50.320 --> 11:52.180
I'll tell you everything slowly.

174
11:52.480 --> 11:54.890
Calm down first.

175
12:01.710 --> 12:03.760
[Herod, I'm on the roof of your hospital. If you don't come in 5 minutes, I'll jump.]

176
12:13.790 --> 12:14.870
Herod.

177
12:18.440 --> 12:20.040
What are you doing right now?

178
12:26.780 --> 12:28.750
What are you trying to do, you bastard?

179
12:28.750 --> 12:30.880
You should be thanking me, Hanyul.

180
12:31.190 --> 12:32.640
What? You bastard!

181
12:33.260 --> 12:36.120
I was really the one taking care of Adolph all along.

182
12:37.010 --> 12:40.030
It was that guy Lee Won who suddenly took him away.

183
12:41.560 --> 12:43.810
Then why didn't you tell me before?

184
12:44.460 --> 12:47.050
Even if you were scared, you shouldn't have kept it a secret.

185
12:47.050 --> 12:48.290
If you knew,

186
12:50.580 --> 12:52.100
you would have gone to him.

187
12:53.670 --> 12:55.680
If you went to him,

188
12:57.220 --> 12:59.370
I would become useless again.

189
12:59.840 --> 13:01.900
Is that why you made Adolph like that?

190
13:02.920 --> 13:04.950
He was your friend!

191
13:05.390 --> 13:08.850
How many times do I have to say it wasn't me for you to believe it?

192
13:09.870 --> 13:11.580
Still denying...

193
13:12.040 --> 13:13.510
I saw you.

194
13:15.120 --> 13:17.740
I saw you were there, you bastard!

195
13:21.510 --> 13:23.330
Go to hell, you bastard!

196
13:23.910 --> 13:24.860
This is amazing.

197
13:25.090 --> 13:26.650
Are you filming?

198
13:29.420 --> 13:31.630
The reason I went there...

199
13:31.880 --> 13:33.600
I mean, I was there for...

200
13:33.730 --> 13:35.480
You wanted Adolph dead.

201
13:36.190 --> 13:37.390
Didn't you?

202
13:37.630 --> 13:38.930
Say it.

203
13:39.690 --> 13:41.630
Herod likes Lee Hanyul.

204
13:41.760 --> 13:44.680
But Lee Hanyul sticks with this guy all day long.

205
13:44.750 --> 13:46.210
This guy is quite likable.

206
13:47.000 --> 13:48.250
Oh, you're here.

207
13:48.910 --> 13:51.170
Look at his face. It's hilarious, right?

208
13:51.710 --> 13:56.420
Dare you say you never had such a thought even for a moment?

209
14:01.750 --> 14:02.950
Hey, hey.

210
14:03.650 --> 14:05.060
Shall we take a photo?

211
14:05.780 --> 14:06.840
Look here.

212
14:10.460 --> 14:11.650
I...

213
14:13.030 --> 14:15.430
I only wanted you to be by my side.

214
14:16.140 --> 14:17.370
I...

215
14:18.570 --> 14:20.540
I've always been by your side.

216
14:21.360 --> 14:23.380
You didn't have to get rid of anyone.

217
14:24.790 --> 14:27.100
I would have walked to your side myself.

218
14:28.540 --> 14:29.900
You're lying.

219
14:31.330 --> 14:33.180
When you needed me,

220
14:33.670 --> 14:35.740
was I ever not by your side?

221
14:36.870 --> 14:38.580
I liked you.

222
14:40.260 --> 14:41.890
Very much.

223
14:45.990 --> 14:47.200
Hanyul.

224
14:48.730 --> 14:50.280
I'm sorry.

225
14:51.130 --> 14:52.330
I liked you too much.

226
14:52.510 --> 14:53.440
No.

227
14:56.740 --> 14:58.370
You didn't like me.

228
14:59.960 --> 15:02.550
You loved the way you looked when you liked me.

229
15:04.950 --> 15:06.050
Hanyul.

230
15:06.750 --> 15:08.440
Let's start over.

231
15:08.960 --> 15:11.390
Adolph, you, and me. Let's start over...

232
15:12.520 --> 15:13.700
No.

233
15:14.890 --> 15:16.250
Over my dead body.

234
15:18.390 --> 15:21.120
Don't ever appear in front of Adolph and me again.

235
15:25.400 --> 15:26.580
Hanyul.

236
15:28.770 --> 15:30.210
Just once...

237
15:30.570 --> 15:32.760
Can you hug me just once?

238
15:33.890 --> 15:35.570
I'm sorry.

239
15:37.560 --> 15:38.880
Hanyul.

240
15:40.490 --> 15:44.510
If you want to apologize, go to Adolph.

241
15:44.830 --> 15:46.340
Don't apologize to me.

242
15:59.780 --> 16:01.070
It's my fault.

243
16:07.880 --> 16:09.380
It's all my fault.

244
16:36.670 --> 16:37.710
Where did you go?

245
16:37.880 --> 16:39.540
You didn't answer your phone.

246
16:40.440 --> 16:41.930
I just went out for a bit.

247
16:42.690 --> 16:43.910
Did...

248
16:46.010 --> 16:47.210
Did you cry?

249
16:47.630 --> 16:49.250
I didn't cry.

250
16:51.280 --> 16:53.420
Do you know how long we've been looking for you?

251
16:53.420 --> 16:55.160
I was only gone for 10 minutes.

252
16:55.520 --> 16:57.600
Not me. It was...

253
17:01.490 --> 17:02.700
Lee Hanyul!

254
17:11.089 --> 17:12.250
Adolph!

255
17:18.920 --> 17:20.960
[Strict bed rest]

256
17:28.550 --> 17:31.130
Hanyul, don't you think I'm really lucky?

257
17:31.270 --> 17:32.460
I heard that if it were anyone else,

258
17:32.460 --> 17:35.460
they would have died on the spot in such a huge traffic accident.

259
17:35.460 --> 17:38.120
I feel like I just woke up from a long sleep.

260
17:38.730 --> 17:41.250
But they said I can't walk yet.

261
17:41.380 --> 17:43.950
Something about lying down for too long or whatever.

262
17:43.950 --> 17:46.660
He still doesn't know what he went through.

263
17:46.810 --> 17:48.580
So I just made up some excuses.

264
17:49.320 --> 17:52.690
Why would you say it was a huge traffic accident where he could've died on the spot.

265
17:52.690 --> 17:55.910
Also, do you know how surprised I was when I opened my eyes?

266
17:56.070 --> 17:59.940
The famous composer Lee Won was right in front of me...

267
18:01.080 --> 18:02.540
Hanyul, you remember, right?

268
18:02.540 --> 18:04.630
I said I wanted to be a composer like Lee Won.

269
18:04.630 --> 18:06.310
Of course, I remember.

270
18:08.580 --> 18:12.220
I wrote a song called "Sound of Dawn."

271
18:12.360 --> 18:14.700
Could you listen to it,

272
18:14.970 --> 18:15.910
please?

273
18:16.640 --> 18:18.020
Ah, sure.

274
18:18.310 --> 18:19.600
I'm all ears.

275
18:23.160 --> 18:24.720
By the way, where is Herod?

276
18:26.290 --> 18:27.400
Ah...

277
18:27.730 --> 18:28.670
Herod.

278
18:28.780 --> 18:29.940
Herod.

279
18:30.180 --> 18:33.980
Seriously, this guy Herod. His good friend woke up after a few years.

280
18:34.730 --> 18:36.000
Where did he go?

281
18:36.760 --> 18:38.190
Herod... Well...

282
18:38.370 --> 18:39.410
He's dead.

283
18:40.280 --> 18:41.390
Huh?

284
18:42.300 --> 18:43.160
That's not it.

285
18:43.340 --> 18:44.290
I mean, Herod...

286
18:44.410 --> 18:46.450
I should have killed him, but I couldn't do it.

287
18:46.450 --> 18:47.660
He'll be dead soon.

288
18:49.860 --> 18:52.670
Herod was super worried about you.

289
18:52.790 --> 18:56.650
He probably didn't come because he wasn't told that you're awake yet.

290
18:57.180 --> 18:59.460
Although I don't remember clearly,

291
18:59.640 --> 19:01.300
in my last memories, Herod...

292
19:01.560 --> 19:02.730
That's it.

293
19:05.230 --> 19:07.150
Let's stop here for today.

294
19:07.890 --> 19:10.570
Slowly recall the rest later on.

295
19:10.940 --> 19:12.810
Mm, got it.

296
19:14.670 --> 19:16.180
But thank god!

297
19:18.430 --> 19:20.060
He's on strict bed rest.

298
19:24.010 --> 19:25.490
-Have you been well? -Yeah.

299
19:25.320 --> 19:26.730
[Secretary]

300
19:26.650 --> 19:27.570
Are you singing?

301
19:27.570 --> 19:28.460
I'm still singing.

302
19:28.460 --> 19:29.240
What about composing?

303
19:29.240 --> 19:30.370
I'm also composing.

304
19:30.450 --> 19:31.980
-You're composing? -Yeah.

305
19:31.980 --> 19:33.310
What are you composing?

306
19:42.730 --> 19:43.970
No.

307
19:45.160 --> 19:46.700
Over my dead body.

308
19:47.870 --> 19:50.600
Don't ever appear in front of Adolph and me again.

309
20:01.340 --> 20:02.570
Hello, it's me.

310
20:05.160 --> 20:09.220
Do you still have the phone numbers of those classmates from high school?

311
20:14.220 --> 20:15.340
Oh, okay.

312
20:16.570 --> 20:18.730
You said you found those bastard classmates?

313
20:18.730 --> 20:19.710
Yes.

314
20:20.620 --> 20:23.220
Right at the entrance of our company building.

315
20:23.950 --> 20:26.190
I clearly hit harder, idiot.

316
20:26.320 --> 20:29.650
Looks like they are here to extort some money with the video.

317
20:31.170 --> 20:32.200
Yes.

318
20:35.600 --> 20:36.640
Then let's play rock-paper-scissors. Damn it.

319
20:36.640 --> 20:37.360
Why play rock-paper-scissors?

320
20:37.360 --> 20:38.380
-No. -Just play rock-paper-scissors.

321
20:38.380 --> 20:39.710
Rock-paper-scissors.

322
20:39.760 --> 20:40.700
Damn it.

323
20:41.560 --> 20:42.830
You scared me.

324
20:43.890 --> 20:45.020
Who are you?

325
21:01.510 --> 21:02.730
So what?

326
21:03.420 --> 21:05.810
Lee Hanyul isn't in this video.

327
21:06.360 --> 21:08.580
Well...

328
21:08.730 --> 21:10.490
H-Herod is in it.

329
21:10.680 --> 21:11.590
Yeah.

330
21:12.440 --> 21:13.230
Herod?

331
21:13.400 --> 21:14.170
Yes.

332
21:14.280 --> 21:16.300
Herod is also a singer under your company, right?

333
21:16.300 --> 21:18.860
Compared to Lee Hanyul, Herod is more popular, right?

334
21:18.860 --> 21:21.720
It will probably bring a bigger blow to the company.

335
21:28.190 --> 21:30.360
So no matter what,

336
21:30.870 --> 21:33.710
your claims that the video captured Lee Hanyul

337
21:34.160 --> 21:37.050
and that he killed his friend

338
21:37.520 --> 21:40.020
are all lies you made up.

339
21:41.740 --> 21:43.470
If you don't want it, forget it.

340
21:43.490 --> 21:44.710
Hey, let's go.

341
21:44.990 --> 21:46.510
Herod called just now, right?

342
21:46.510 --> 21:47.460
Yeah.

343
21:47.620 --> 21:49.740
Let's go sell it to him. Let's go.

344
21:54.260 --> 21:55.330
What are you doing?

345
21:55.460 --> 21:57.320
Didn't you say you don't need this video?

346
21:57.320 --> 21:58.560
I mean.

347
21:58.770 --> 22:01.170
The fact that Lee Hanyul isn't in this video

348
22:01.280 --> 22:04.480
is enough to prove he has nothing to do with this incident.

349
22:07.850 --> 22:09.180
Time to take a beating.

350
22:10.150 --> 22:11.310
I promise you.

351
22:13.960 --> 22:15.860
As long as you stay by my side,

352
22:16.010 --> 22:18.200
I won't let anyone get hurt.

353
22:31.520 --> 22:34.820
You should be glad I'm much easier to talk to lately.

354
22:35.340 --> 22:36.410
Go.

355
22:36.600 --> 22:38.580
Hurry up. Hurry up.

356
22:55.430 --> 22:57.060
These rascals—

357
23:16.520 --> 23:18.790
With this, Hanyul can live.

358
23:20.870 --> 23:23.140
Without this, you can live, right?

359
23:31.690 --> 23:32.970
Take it.

360
23:41.350 --> 23:43.650
This is your only chance.

361
24:04.520 --> 24:08.080
[The Sound of Sugar Cubes]

362
24:07.980 --> 24:09.580
It's been a while, Herod.

363
24:09.720 --> 24:11.190
It's me, Shinyoung.

364
24:11.380 --> 24:13.200
Ah, you don't remember?

365
24:13.400 --> 24:14.400
That's quite sad.

366
24:14.570 --> 24:16.560
If I say this, will you remember something?

367
24:16.560 --> 24:18.650
The one who was with Adolph at the end.

368
24:18.820 --> 24:20.570
I see you're quite popular lately.

369
24:20.570 --> 24:21.950
You must have made a lot of money, right?

370
24:21.950 --> 24:24.980
How dare you trick me, you bastard.

371
24:26.330 --> 24:28.700
Go die.

372
24:30.310 --> 24:31.340
Lee Won!

373
24:31.490 --> 24:32.540
[Hanyul]

374
24:33.090 --> 24:34.810
Fake contract for performance fees,

375
24:34.810 --> 24:36.320
paper company outsourcing contracts,

376
24:36.320 --> 24:37.550
operating a business under a borrowed name,

377
24:37.550 --> 24:38.680
[Fake contract for performance fees, paper company outsourcing contracts, operating a business under a borrowed name, designing a slush fund structure]

378
24:37.620 --> 24:39.710
designing a slush fund structure.

379
24:39.870 --> 24:43.410
The Lee Won I know does whatever the boss tells him to do.
